{"id": "EUVD-2026-104397", "enisaUuid": "be4be993-1576-3a41-a3ff-8eb2607e1337", "description": "Semaphore UI through 2.19.16 contains a remote code execution vulnerability that allows users with the task_runner role to override protected Ansible variables by supplying arbitrary keys in the task environment JSON. Attackers can POST tasks setting ansible_ssh_common_args with a ProxyCommand or ansible_connection=local to execute commands as the Semaphore server user, exposing encryption keys, SSH keys and stored secrets.", "datePublished": "2026-10-19T15:28:55", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T17:40:14", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/semaphoreui/semaphore/pull/3888", "https://github.com/semaphoreui/semaphore/blob/v2.19.16/services/tasks/TaskRunner.go#L395-L431", "https://github.com/semaphoreui/semaphore/blob/v2.19.16/api/projects/tasks.go#L39-L75", "https://github.com/semaphoreui/semaphore", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/semaphore-ui-through-2.19.16-rce-via-task-environment-ansible-variable-override"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-112305", "GHSA-6cr7-7xqc-c37c"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.56, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "7c483df9-0dd3-3a60-b7ab-faaf82caf825", "product": {"name": "Semaphore UI", "vendor": {"name": "semaphoreui"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642.19.16"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "f1362ca0-f466-358e-bea4-72a31a36ddae", "vendor": {"name": "semaphoreui"}}], "isExploited": false}